What are some best practices for optimizing JavaScript code for performance? Can you provide an example of how you would refactor a piece of code to improve its performance? 
Here is some JavaScript code as input:
function fibonacci(n) {
  if (n < 2) {
    return n;
  } else {
    return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
  }
}
console.log(fibonacci(10)); // Output: 55
How would you optimize this code for better performance?

