Step 1: Factor out 5 from both terms in the numerator and denominator.
\begin{aligned} \frac{5x + 6y}{5x + 5y} &= \frac{5(x + \frac{6}{5}y)}{5(x + y)} \\ \end{aligned}
Step 2: Simplify by canceling out the common factor of 5 in the numerator and denominator.
\begin{aligned} \frac{5x + 6y}{5x + 5y} &= \frac{\cancel{5}(x + \frac{6}{5}y)}{\cancel{5}(x + y)} \\ &= \frac{x + \frac{6}{5}y}{x + y} \end{aligned}
