How can we modify the SQL query to retrieve the names of all customers who have made purchases of multiple items with a total price over $1000 at the same time from our sales database? We can achieve this by creating a subquery that counts the number of unique items each customer has purchased. Here's an example code:
SELECT DISTINCT customer.name, purchase.date, item.name
FROM customer
JOIN purchase ON customer.customer_id = purchase.customer_id
JOIN item ON purchase.item_id = item.item_id
JOIN sale ON sale.purchase_id = purchase.purchase_id
WHERE sale.price IN (
    SELECT price
    FROM sale
    WHERE customer_id IN (
        SELECT customer_id
        FROM purchase
        GROUP BY customer_id
        HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT item_id) >= 2 AND SUM(price) > 1000
    )
)
ORDER BY purchase.date ASC;
